eline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1726,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[1855,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[1846,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[1907,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[1848,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[1856,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[1859,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[1903,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1727,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[1852,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[1849,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[1847,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[1857,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1758,"✅ Custom domains"],[1759,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1363,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1617,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. Undo / Redo, Zoom In / Out / Reset)"],[1616,"✅ For grouped contextual actions — two or more closely related actions that belong together (e.g. Bold / Italic / Underline, Align Left / Center / Right)"],[1618,"✅ For multi-select scenarios — when users need to select multiple options simultaneously"],[295,"✅ For selecting multiple independent options"],[1362,"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"],[297,"✅ For toggling settings or features on/off"],[1757,"✅ Interactive tooltips"],[1756,"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"],[1754,"✅ Single and multi-series support"],[1755,"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"],[298,"✅ When all available options should be visible"],[1100,"✅ When all options should be visible at once"],[1101,"✅ When the decision is important and deserves space"],[1099,"✅ When there are 2-7 mutually exclusive options"],[296,"✅ When users can select zero, one, or many items"],[1103,"❌ For binary yes/no choices (use Checkbox or Toggle instead)"],[1365,"❌ For choosing one of several mutually exclusive options (use `Radio` or `SegmentedController` instead)"],[1620,"❌ For more than 5 choices — cognitive overload; consider a **Select** instead"],[1102,"❌ For more than 7 options (use Select instead)"],[1623,"❌ For mutually exclusive content views (e.g. Monthly / Yearly) — use **SegmentedController** instead"],[299,"❌ For mutually exclusive options (use Radio instead)"],[1364,"❌ For selections that require a \"Save\" or \"Submit\" action (use `Checkbox` instead)"],[300,"❌ For simple on/off toggles without labels (use Toggle/Switch instead)"],[1619,"❌ For unrelated actions that perform disconnected tasks without shared context"],[1621,"❌ When actions require strong visual distinction (e.g. Save vs. Delete)"],[1622,"❌ When selecting an option leads to a different page or work